<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The PWA's maskable icon, sized for Android's adaptive-icon geometry.

  An adaptive icon layer is 108dp, of which a launcher mask shows at most the middle 72dp; the
  outer 18dp on each side is there to be cropped and to give the launcher room to parallax. The
  artwork in icon-512-maskable.png is a rounded-square badge that occupies the middle 71.3% of
  its own canvas (measured: content spans 365 of 512 px, on a border of one flat colour).

  Drawn full-bleed - which is what a maskable icon nominally allows, and what the tooling that
  turns a PWA into an APK does by default - that badge lands at 0.713 x 108dp = 77.0dp, wider
  than the 72dp a mask is allowed to show, and a round launcher mask cuts through the
  ANTI-FRAUD line under the bear. Inset by 4% the badge is 0.713 x 99.4dp = 70.8dp: it fits
  inside the mask viewport, so a circle can only ever take the badge's own rounded corners, and
  the bear, 反詐騙 and ANTI-FRAUD stay whole under every mask shape. AppIconTest measures the
  artwork and re-derives that bound, so redrawing the PWA icon wider forces the inset to be
  revisited instead of silently clipping the new art.

  The 4% of margin this leaves is filled by @color/ic_launcher_background, which is the flat
  colour the artwork's own border already is - so the seam is invisible and a mask that shows
  more than 72dp shows more of the same navy.

  android:inset takes a fraction from API 26, and this drawable is only ever reached through
  mipmap-anydpi-v26, so the fraction is always understood.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_maskable"
    android:inset="4%" />
